From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:46:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 83/83] fix(ci): skip the Manifold inference gate loudly when
 config is absent (gcp-oz57)

Four consecutive scheduled Supported Pack Nightly runs (34128826579,
34031160049, 33963223598, 33871938839) failed on one identical signature: all
six pack jobs died at step 11 `Validate Manifold Claude configuration` with
"Missing OLLAMA_API_KEY GitHub secret", because this fork holds no Actions
configuration at all -- re-read at the API 2026-09-07, `actions/secrets` and
`actions/variables` both report total_count 0. `static pack flow contracts` was
green in every one of those runs.

A job that is always red is read by nobody and is indistinguishable from a job
that has gone red for a NEW reason. That is the cost this change removes, and
it is all it removes: this is an INTERIM MITIGATION, not a fix. It makes an
unrunnable gate legible; it does not make the gate run. Whether this fork
should hold Manifold credentials at all is the root question and it stays OPEN
on gcp-gmkx (mayor ruling on gcp-gmkx notes, 2026-09-07T17:26:41Z: "A0 RULED:
option (b), as an explicit INTERIM").

New `.github/scripts/manifold-config-status.sh` is the single source of truth
for "is the Manifold config present": it reads the six env names the workflows
map their two secrets and four variables into, prints `present=` and `missing=`
for $GITHUB_OUTPUT, and ALWAYS exits 0. It decides; it does not enforce. When
config is absent it writes a loud notice -- naming every missing value and
citing gcp-gmkx -- to both the job log and $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY, so a skipped
run is never a silent green. A silent green would be strictly worse than
today's honest red.

`if: secrets.X != ''` was not an option and this was verified rather than
assumed: GitHub's context-availability table does not offer `secrets` to
`jobs.<job_id>.steps.<step_id>.if`, so that expression never evaluates. `env`
is available, but an `if:` cannot write the summary the ruling requires and it
would spread the six-name list to a third copy.

Deviation from the bead's design, flagged for review: the bead placed the
detection step in the nightly immediately after `Decide manual subset`, i.e.
BEFORE `Check out gascity-packs`. The script lives in the repo, so at that
point it is not yet on disk. It runs immediately after that checkout instead --
the earliest position at which it can work -- and a test asserts that ordering
so the constraint cannot be lost later. The inference workflow checks out
first, so there the bead's placement stands unchanged.

Scope held deliberately tight. The bodies of both `Validate Manifold Claude
configuration` steps are byte-identical -- only their `if:` lines changed, and
a test asserts all eight checks survive. `static pack flow contracts` is
untouched and a test asserts it never acquires a skip condition. No `runs-on:`
changed. No secret or variable value was created or guessed. The install steps
still run: the six jobs keep paying ~3m of installs for a run whose only
meaningful step now skips, which is worth its own bead on a pool that has
already had capacity evictions (gcp-m0ei) but is not this one.

Validation. The positive branch cannot be demonstrated live on this fork --
there are no credentials and inventing them is the very question gcp-gmkx
holds -- so extracting the decision into a script is what makes the skip
falsifiable instead of unfalsifiable-by-construction. Six new tests in
tests/test_gascity_pack_inference_gate.py, which `static pack flow contracts`
already runs, cover both branches with env set by the test, the partial-config
case, and the workflow gating (parsed as YAML, not grepped, so a folded scalar
that lost its second clause is caught). Each was shown RED against the
regression it guards: dropping a gate clause, making the script enforce rather
than decide, and deleting a validation check. 158 passed, 5936 subtests.
go vet clean, golangci-lint 0 issues, go test ok, shellcheck clean.
